  "scope": "The original formula (T) needs a typed source at an arrow. At any original signature/closed window and genuine type, the guard holds exactly on actual canonical addresses of that result type. A positive arrow guard supplies its original same-context fresh computable variable, successful canonical application, and typed codomain at the literal output. Two serialized primitive programs compute the guard and optional fresh address on every numeric input. Open object derivability is separate.",
